    deck: "Food and drink",
    body: `
<p>Ordering in Chinese is short and direct. You already have the tools: <b>要</b> <i>yào</i> (want), numbers, and measure words.</p>
<h3>Getting attention</h3>
<p>In a restaurant, call the server <b>服务员</b> <i>fúwùyuán</i>. It is neutral and normal, not rude. Avoid <b>小姐</b>: in the mainland it can now suggest a sex worker.</p>
{{ex:服务员！|Fúwùyuán!|Excuse me! (calling the server)}}
<h3>Three ways to order</h3>
<p>English softens an order with "could I have" or "I'll have". Chinese has three common frames:</p>
<ul><li><b>我要</b> <i>wǒ yào</i>…: "I want…". The normal way to order.</li><li><b>来</b> <i>lái</i>…: literally "come", meaning "bring me". Casual and very common.</li><li><b>请给我</b> <i>qǐng gěi wǒ</i>…: "please give me". The softest.</li></ul>
{{ex:我要一碗面条。|Wǒ yào yì wǎn miàntiáo.|I'd like a bowl of noodles.}}
{{ex:来两杯奶茶。|Lái liǎng bēi nǎichá.|Two milk teas, please.}}
{{ex:请给我一杯水。|Qǐng gěi wǒ yì bēi shuǐ.|Could I have a glass of water, please?}}
<h3>Measure words on the menu</h3>
<p>Whatever you order, the number needs its measure word: <b>碗</b> <i>wǎn</i> for a bowl, <b>杯</b> for a cup or glass, <b>瓶</b> <i>píng</i> for a bottle, <b>个</b> for things like dumplings or buns. English "two milk teas" has none; Chinese must say "two cups of milk tea".</p>
<h3>Spicy or not</h3>
<p>Many dishes are spicy by default. <b>辣</b> <i>là</i> means spicy; <b>不要辣的</b> means "not the spicy kind". If you like a little heat, say <b>微辣</b> <i>wēilà</i> (mildly spicy).</p>
{{ex:不要辣的。|Bú yào là de.|Not spicy, please.}}
<h3>Tasty, and paying</h3>
<p><b>好吃</b> <i>hǎochī</i> is "good to eat" and <b>好喝</b> <i>hǎohē</i> is "good to drink": English says "delicious" for both, Chinese doesn't. To pay, call the server and say <b>买单</b> <i>mǎidān</i>. To take leftovers home, or to order to go, say <b>打包</b> <i>dǎbāo</i>.</p>
{{ex:这个很好吃！|Zhège hěn hǎochī!|This is delicious!}}
{{ex:服务员，买单！|Fúwùyuán, mǎidān!|Check, please!}}
<div class="tbl"><table><tr><th>You want to say</th><th>Chinese</th></tr><tr><td>A bowl of noodles, please.</td><td class="k">我要一碗面条。</td></tr><tr><td>Not spicy.</td><td class="k">不要辣的。</td></tr><tr><td>To go, please.</td><td class="k">打包。</td></tr><tr><td>Check, please!</td><td class="k">买单！</td></tr></table></div>
<div class="tip"><b>Most common mistake:</b> ordering with a number and no measure word, the English way. <b>我要两奶茶。</b> → <b>我要两杯奶茶。</b></div>
`,
